ence-SsupporTed Automated NutRiTional Intervention on LDL cholesterol Control in Patients with Familial Hypercholesterolaemia (iSTART-FH): protocol for a randomised controlled trial#🟡 Genel Bilgiler (Sarı)":[35,37],"#Effects of artificial intelligence-SsupporTed Automated NutRiTional Intervention on LDL cholesterol Control in Patients with Familial Hypercholesterolaemia (iSTART-FH): protocol for a randomised controlled trial#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)":[38,40],"#Effects of artificial intelligence-SsupporTed Automated NutRiTional Intervention on LDL cholesterol Control in Patients with Familial Hypercholesterolaemia (iSTART-FH): protocol for a randomised controlled trial#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)#{1}":[39,40],"#Effects of artificial intelligence-SsupporTed Automated NutRiTional Intervention on LDL cholesterol Control in Patients with Familial Hypercholesterolaemia (iSTART-FH): protocol for a randomised controlled trial#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[41,43],"#Effects of artificial intelligence-SsupporTed Automated NutRiTional Intervention on LDL cholesterol Control in Patients with Familial Hypercholesterolaemia (iSTART-FH): protocol for a randomised controlled trial#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[44,46],"#Effects of artificial intelligence-SsupporTed Automated NutRiTional Intervention on LDL cholesterol Control in Patients with Familial Hypercholesterolaemia (iSTART-FH): protocol for a randomised controlled trial#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[47,48]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/YDTQ28FB","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/KDUKPF2C?page=1&annotation=F9QC97G9","line":39},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/KDUKPF2C?page=1&annotation=RZXDQM4P","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"Effects of artificial intelligence-SsupporTed Automated NutRiTional Intervention on LDL cholesterol Control in Patients with Familial Hypercholesterolaemia (iSTART-FH): protocol for a randomised controlled trial","Authors":"Hayato Tada, Hirofumi Okada, Akihiro Nomura, Soichiro Usui, Kenji Sakata, Kenshi Hayashi, Noboru Fujino, Ayaka Yasugi, Shizuko Takahara, Yasuhito Imai, Masayuki Takamura, Masa-aki Kawashiri","Year":2021,"DOI":"10.1136/bmjopen-2021-053453","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"This study aims to test the hypothesis that AI-supported nutritional counselling is more effective in reducing LDL cholesterol than the in-person, face-to-face method in terms of improving LDL cholesterol control in patients with FH.This is a single-centre, unblinded, cross-over, randomised controlled study comparing the efficacy of AI-supported automated nutrition therapy with that of conventional human nutrition counselling in patients with FH.","Findings":"","Conclusions":"","Limitations":"","User_Notes":"yöntem makalesi  dyt karlılaştırması var  bulgular yayımlanmış mı bak  prompt yok, gerekli mi doğrula"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"p3swko","at":1774939670419}},"smart_blocks:tadaEffectsArtificialIntelligenceSsupporTed2021a.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.0078654,0.03812619,-0.01984969,0.02664447,-0.01620893,-0.02459039,-0.01706035,0.05059195,-0.00532166,-0.06294974,-0.01089596,-0.1109905,0.04043156,0.01467847,0.02368613,-0.03602818,0.02284994,0.00077198,-0.05343008,0.03658529,0.04716347,-0.04432435,-0.0075427,-0.03305013,0.01374133,0.02747228,-0.00597214,-0.10989238,-0.06650017,-0.20654875,0.05934271,-0.05515403,0.03474575,-0.02469738,-0.03080738,0.00265073,0.00576804,0.02884858,-0.01466718,0.02566848,0.0635574,-0.00868115,0.03232963,0.00231963,0.02239357,-0.0436023,-0.03305105,0.00311825,-0.03198013,-0.01616393,-0.05947454,0.0124282,0.04415738,0.0331987,0.01680512,0.02457974,0.05887253,0.05093737,0.04123533,0.03604978,-0.00284807,0.06633694,-0.2016239,0.12626317,0.03203597,0.0